      "blocked_by": "roadmap:p1-schema-products-variants-taxonomy",
      "body": "Caught 2026-08-08 when `Category.dc.html` was rebuilt around \"Vegetables & Fruits\" that neither Home nor Categories listed. **Audited 2026-08-09 and found to be un-evaluable, which is the more useful answer** — see 1.46. `Categories.dc.html` passes a category *name* through to `Category.dc.html` rather than hardcoding one, so the reachability half holds; but \"every category with stock\" cannot be computed, because no product anywhere is assigned to a category. Reopen this once 1.46 gives the taxonomy a single origin. **Half-answerable as of 2026-08-17:** §7 now authors the join, so \"every category with stock\" is computable for the first time — and by that table all 13 categories hold stock, which is the state this case wants. **Answerable at last as of 2026-08-17, and it half-holds** — 1.46 closed, so the surfaces now read the table rather than their own literals, and what can be checked is finally what the surfaces *do*. The reachability half holds outright: `Categories.dc.html` derives all 13 tiles from §7 and each opens a Category page, so no Category page is unreachable and none is reachable only by a demo tweak. **The stock half does not**, and now for a stated reason rather than an un-evaluable one: the customer build built no availability logic at all, so \"only categories with stock appear\" is satisfied by the demo lists happening to stock all 13 rather than by anything computing it — `admin.md` §6 requires it be computed from available-to-sell and never a manual flag. One category proved the point during that build: re-filing `Salt & Sugar` to its §7 home emptied Masala & Oil, and the derived tile went on rendering, because nothing checks. It was fixed by stocking the category, which is the right fix for the data and no fix at all for the mechanism. This closes when a surface computes the rule. Worth stating precisely, since this case is about the prototypes: Home & Office having had no reachable product was **not** a breach of this rule's letter — an empty category appearing violates neither \"every category with stock appears\" nor \"every Category page is reachable\". It was evidence for 1.46, and it is now moot.",
