      "body": "Guards the corrected §10 rule against the two lists drifting apart again. **Audited 2026-08-09: the lists match, the mapping is unexercised, and one status has nowhere to land.** `Admin Orders.dc.html` defines exactly `new · packing · ready · ofd · delivered · cancelled` and the customer tracker in `Checkout.dc.html` defines exactly `Placed · Packed · Out for delivery · Delivered` — five statuses plus cancelled against four nodes, which is §10's table precisely. But no code implements the mapping (the two surfaces share no state; the tracker reads a four-value demo prop), and **cancelled has no customer-side rendering at all**: `Orders.dc.html`'s `buildOrder` can only ever produce \"Out for delivery\" or \"Delivered\", so the one admin status §10 says must *replace* the progress bar has nothing to replace it with. The counts agree; the behaviour is not demonstrated. **Closed 2026-08-10**: `Orders.dc.html` now renders four card states — out for delivery, delivered, cancelled and couldn't-deliver — each a dot plus a label, and **neither cancelled nor couldn't-deliver draws the progress strip**, which is the card-level echo of those states replacing the bar. Every admin status now has somewhere on the customer surface to land. The two surfaces still share no state, which is a prototype fact rather than a spec one.",
