      "body": "The shop opened in 2026, so year-on-year has no baseline until Aug 2027 and month-on-month has none in the first month; those tiles state why rather than showing `—`, `0%`, or a flat line, and start appearing unremarked once the period is real. The no-zero-walls rule applied to time. Verified 2026-08-09 — the reworked Dashboard renders **both states on one screen**: month-on-month shows a real delta (July 2026 ₹95,400 vs June 2026 ₹83,100, +15% — arithmetic checked) while year-on-year reads *\"No August 2025 to compare — the shop opened in March 2026\"* with no dash, zero, or flat line. Extended the same day with the **like-for-like span rule** (§5): a baseline that exists but is a different length is still a lie, so month-to-date compares against the same days of the prior month (1–8 Aug vs 1–8 Jul), never against a whole month.",
