      "body": "Raised 2026-08-09 by the netting build, which had to approximate the COGS reversal at the month's overall margin rate (≈23.3%) because no per-product cost data existed in the prototypes. Closed the same day: batch costs now reach every catalogue product from `Purchases.dc.html`'s goods receipts, and today's ₹157 of refunds reverses **₹126 exactly** — one Amul Butter at its ₹52 batch cost plus one Lakadong Turmeric at ₹74 — stated on both sale drawers and in the return preview, never a rate applied to ₹157. The consequence is the point: the gross-profit tile stopped being a hardcoded ₹5,305 at +22% and became a derived ₹3,810 at −12%, with the tile itself saying which part is exact (7–8 Aug, from the register's real batch costs) and which is approximated (1–6 Aug, at that same cost ratio). An invented number was replaced by a real one that tells a different story.",
