      "body": "§11's trigger previously swallowed zero, so nine rows mixed \"reorder soon\" with \"already losing sales\" under the milder label while §7 treated them as distinct statuses. Ruled and built 2026-08-09 — the correction build on **Sonnet 5 High** split the kind across both screens. Verified at source: the partition is mutually exclusive (`avail <= 0` → out, `else if (avail <= reorder)` → low), both kinds carry `kindLabel: 'State'` and `closeable: false`, and the new kind arrived with its Alert preferences toggle in the same change set (`kindOn` gains `out: true`, `kindPrefDefs` gains the row) rather than raising alerts nobody could route. Counts recomputed independently from both files: Low stock 3, Out of stock 6, open total unchanged at 19. *(Boundary moved 2026-08-18: out of stock became the physical fact `on hand ≤ 0` and **held** split off the promised-but-present case, so the partition verified above describes the pre-held rule, which the prototypes still compute — spec-first work, prototypes lag.)*",
