      "body": "Verified 2026-08-09 at source: both `Admin.dc.html` and `Admin Reports.dc.html` compute `(onHand − reserved) <= reorder`. §11 had said \"on hand\", contradicting §7; the prototypes had used the right number all along and the document was corrected to match. Latent rather than visible — both bases return 9 against today's data. *(Amended 2026-08-18, PR 2 of the Phase 1 design: this case's rule now holds for **low stock** only — out of stock became `on hand ≤ 0`, the physical fact, with §7's new **held** state taking the ATS-only case, and §11's stock rows now name §7's statuses instead of restating conditions, so this table has nothing left to diverge on. The never-the-raw-balance reasoning survives where selling is the question; the empty-shelf question was never about what could be sold.)*",
