      "body": "Reachability overlaps — one customer opted into three channels counts three times — while the send plan is disjoint and sums to the recipient count, because each recipient gets exactly one message on their highest consented channel (WhatsApp → SMS → push). Found 2026-08-09: §13 illustrated the split with \"890 reachable by SMS · 142 on WhatsApp · 604 have push enabled\", which overlaps, while the dashboard's own figures sum to the recipient count. The build followed the dashboard, found it could not also honour the example, and named the contradiction rather than picking one silently. §13 now defines both and specifies the precedence order the build had to invent.",
