      "body": "A counter sale or void always posts at the store, an order commit always at the warehouse, and neither till nor packer may draw on the other place's count — an empty shelf beside a full warehouse is a transfer to make, never an override to grant. One consequence worth testing on its own: §10's till-vs-packer oversell race is walled off, and what remains is a ledger overstating a shelf (a wrong count, damage found at picking, a transfer that moved promised stock). Added 2026-08-18; open until a surface computes it. **The wall is enforced at the only layer that exists as of 2026-08-18 (#76)**: `movementProblems` refuses a counter-sale or void anywhere but the store and an order-commit anywhere but the warehouse, tested both ways. 🟡 because what is missing is a till and a packer to point at it — no surface posts movements yet.",
