      "body": "`clears_week` and `needed_week` are typed into each record's frontmatter, and the Schedule's table is the origin they came from — so today they agree because they were copied carefully, not because anything checks. That is the shape of 1.46's defect and it is live in this folder. Closes when `status.py` parses the README's registration table and fails on disagreement, the way `check_taxonomy_join.py` parses §7's. Deliberately not built yet: the Schedule's table is prose-formatted and a parser for it is a real piece of work, and one honest ❌ is better than a parser that half-works.",
