      "body": "A fourth view (month grid, Monday weeks, ‹ today › nav) whose every element traces to a real field: authored `start`/`due` bars from board.json, real spans between a record's own `started`/`ended` dates, open waits hatched from the real start to the record's clears-week expectation (or today if later, so a late wait visibly overruns), and ◆ markers on the last day of each `needed_week` — labelled \"needed W*n*\", never \"due\", because it is the record's claim. An undated item is absent, not estimated. Added 2026-08-19 with the view. **The generator's five refusals are unit-tested** (malformed date, due-before-start, a schedule on done work, and — the one that earns the feature — a due past the item's own needed-by week, refused as two authored facts in contradiction; `test_build_tracker`, 73 tests). 🧪 for the render half, the 4.20 method: `calendarSpans` extracted verbatim into node and run against the real `board.data.js` — every span traces to its field, plan spans equal their authored dates exactly, markers land on `week1 + 7n − 1` days, done items raise no marker, and all 166 dateless items are absent — plus an eyeball of the rendered month. Scheduling is board.json-only by design; the page never writes.",
