      "ask_text": "Hello — following on about HSN codes. Once we know the digit count, I need the actual codes for the products we sell.\n\nI'm going to pull our full product list out of the system we use now and send it over as a spreadsheet. If that list already has HSN codes on it, could you just check them and tell me which ones are wrong? That would be much quicker than starting from nothing.\n\nIf it doesn't have them, could you fill in the HSN code and GST rate against each line? Doing it in batches as you get time is completely fine — I'll record whatever arrives and leave the rest blank until it does.\n\nPlease don't estimate any of them. A wrong HSN looks exactly like a right one, and it would sit in our invoices unnoticed. Thank you.",
      "blocked_by": "ops:owner-catalogue-export",
      "body": "**Who:** Accountant\n\n**Blocked on the export, as of 2026-08-18 — do not send this yet.** See `owner-catalogue-export.md`.\n\n**Check this first — it may shrink the ask to almost nothing.** The catalogue is **not** the 60 products in the prototypes; those are demo data invented to build screens against, and none of them is meant to reach the real system. The real seed comes from **exporting the shop's current system** and importing it here. So before asking anyone for codes, look at that export: if it already carries HSN codes and tax rates, this question changes from *\"please supply codes for every product\"* to *\"please confirm these are right\"* — a different and far smaller favour, and one far likelier to come back.\n\n**No value may be invented, by anyone, at any point.** Products carry no HSN until it comes from the export or from the accountant, and the prototype renders the field empty rather than plausible.\n\nThis is stronger than the GSTIN lesson rather than equal to it: the retired GSTIN placeholder at least **failed its own check digit**, so a validator could have caught it. **An HSN has no check digit at all** — a wrong one is indistinguishable from a right one by inspection, and it misstates tax liability rather than looking untidy.\n\nArrives in batches. Record what has landed; leave the rest empty.\n\n## Where it stands\n\nNot asked.\n\n*Append dated lines. Record the answer verbatim — a paraphrase of a number is a new number.*",
