      "ask_text": "Hello — a small decision about where the project's code lives.\n\nThe code is in a private repository on a free plan. On that plan I can't switch on the safety setting that stops bad code being merged into the main branch. There are two ways to fix it: pay for GitHub Pro, which is a few dollars a month, or make the repository public so anyone can read it.\n\nThere's no rush and nothing is broken — the checks all still run and I can see when something fails. It's just that nothing currently *stops* a mistake going in.\n\nWhich would you prefer? If we go with Pro I'll set it up; if public, I'll check nothing private is in there first. Thank you.",
