      "ask_text": "Hello — I need to check something before I apply for the app store accounts.\n\nOur GST registration shows the business as a sole proprietorship rather than a partnership firm. Apple and Google both offer two kinds of developer account: an organisation account, and a personal one.\n\nAn organisation account needs a D-U-N-S number, which takes a few weeks to get. A personal account doesn't need one, but the apps then publish under a personal name instead of \"Convenience Corner\", and Google makes new personal accounts run a two-week test with a dozen testers before going live.\n\nCan a sole proprietorship register as an organisation with them, and what documents would they want? If you're not certain, I'd rather ask Apple and Google support directly than guess — the D-U-N-S is the longest wait in the whole project and I don't want to start it if we don't need it. Thank you.",
      "body": "**Who:** Owner, with the accountant — and this may need asking of Apple and Google support directly rather than inferred from their documentation.\n\nRaised 2026-08-18, when the new GSTIN `17DSTPM2882N1ZO` changed the entity type. The embedded PAN's fourth character is **`P`, an individual — a sole proprietorship** — where the previous entity's was `F`, a partnership firm.\n\n**Why this blocks the D-U-N-S rather than merely informing it.** A D-U-N-S number is required for **organisation** enrolment and not for individual enrolment. So the question is not \"which is nicer\", it is whether the longest-lead-time item in the whole plan is needed at all. Filing it before the answer is known risks wasted weeks, or an application that describes the entity incorrectly — which is worse, because a corrected D-U-N-S is slower than a first one.\n\n**What to establish, in this order:**\n\n1. **Does Apple's Developer Program accept a sole proprietorship as an organisation?** Apple's organisation enrolment asks for a legal entity name and a D-U-N-S. A proprietorship has **no legal personality separate from its proprietor**, so the \"legal entity name\" is generally the proprietor's own name — which may make the enrolment functionally individual regardless of which path is chosen.\n2. **Does Google Play accept it?** Google distinguishes personal and organisation accounts, and applies the closed-testing requirement (a dozen testers, before production) to new **personal** accounts. Whether a proprietorship counts as an organisation there decides whether that testing requirement lands on this project — which is a schedule item, not just paperwork.\n3. **Can a sole proprietorship obtain a D-U-N-S at all**, and under what name? Dun & Bradstreet does register proprietorships, but the registered name and the shop's trade name may differ, and both stores match the D-U-N-S record against the entity documents.\n\n**What this changes downstream if the answer is \"individual only\":** the apps publish under a **personal name** rather than \"Convenience Corner\"; Google's closed-test requirement applies before production; and the D-U-N-S record in `../registrations/duns.md` becomes unnecessary rather than merely early, which removes roughly four weeks from the critical path in exchange for a worse store listing.\n\n**Do not answer this from documentation alone.** Both stores' published guidance is written for companies and is thin on proprietorships, and the consequence of guessing is measured in weeks. If the accountant cannot answer it definitively, ask each store's support and record what they say verbatim.\n\nThe GSTIN and its structural verification live once in `design-system/pages/admin.md` §5 and are not restated here.\n\n## Field reports, 2026-08-19 — not an answer, but they reshape the ask\n\nA r/iOSProgramming thread ([reddit.com/r/iOSProgramming/comments/1fapajq](https://www.reddit.com/r/iOSProgramming/comments/1fapajq/enroling_in_apple_developer_program_as_a_sole/), opened September 2024, still accumulating reports within weeks of this note) collects first-hand accounts from sole proprietors enrolling on both stores. Forum reports are weaker evidence than documentation, which this record already refuses to trust — they are recorded because they are **consistent across a year, several countries, and both stores**, and because they change what to say to Apple rather than what to believe.\n\n- **Google Play**: the opening poster — a sole proprietor with a GST certificate (legal name, trade name, business address) and a D-U-N-S — enrolled as an **organisation** without difficulty. That would dodge the closed-testing requirement that lands on new personal accounts.\n- **Apple, the expected failure**: organisation enrolment by a sole proprietor trips a standard web error — \"This organization could not be verified as a legal entity\" (Apple's enrolment page) — directing proprietorships to individual enrolment. Every successful report goes through **Apple developer support manually unlocking it**: France (regional email, lifted next day — twice, one as recently as ~3 weeks before this note), Netherlands (resolved during a single phone call), and **one Indian sole proprietorship confirming the same unlock worked**. Support verifies the D-U-N-S record and lifts the block; D&B registers proprietorships as such (one report: number issued in minutes; another needed D&B profile fields corrected first).\n- **The slower alternative**: enrol as an individual first, then ask support to convert to organisation against the D-U-N-S — the opening poster reports a full conversion with all organisation benefits, roughly two weeks and several calls, plus a follow-up to switch the displayed developer name to the trade name. Until conversion completes, the seller name is the proprietor's personal name.\n- **India-specific friction**: one Indian user could not find an Apple India support *phone* number — email and the callback form (`developer.apple.com/contact`) were the available routes.\n- **One unresolved failure** is in the thread too — a migration that stalled on the same legal-entity check after escalation — so the unlock is well-attested, not guaranteed.\n\n**What this changes:** the expected answer shifts from \"possibly individual-only\" to \"organisation enrolment is attainable for a proprietorship via a support override, so the D-U-N-S is likely needed after all\" — see the dated note in `../registrations/duns.md`. The ask to Apple support should therefore be shaped as *\"we are a sole proprietorship with a D-U-N-S, we expect the legal-entity error on organisation enrolment — please verify our D-U-N-S record and unlock it\"*, not as an open question. **What this does not change:** the status below. Nothing has been asked of Apple, Google, or the accountant, and this record still wants each store's own answer verbatim before anything is filed.\n\n## Where it stands\n\nNot asked. Raised the same day the entity changed.\n\n2026-08-19 — Field reports folded in above: sole proprietors do get organisation accounts on both stores, on Apple via a manual support unlock (multi-country, one Indian confirmation). The ask to Apple is reshaped accordingly; still nothing asked.\n\n*Append dated lines. Record the answer verbatim — a paraphrase of a number is a new number, and a paraphrase of a policy is a new policy.*",
