      "ask_text": "",
      "body": "**Gates:** Google Play Console and Apple Developer Program — both, and nothing downstream of either starts without it\n\n**Needs before applying:** Entity documents for the **sole proprietorship** — and first, an answer to whether an organisation account is available at all (see below)\n\n**Blocked on a question, as of 2026-08-18 — do not file this yet.** *(Hold lifted 2026-08-19 by the owner's decision, after the field reports below shifted the trade — the filing proceeds as a sole proprietorship. The paragraphs beneath are kept as the reasoning that held it, not rewritten.)*\n\nThis record previously read that Convenience Corner is a *partnership firm* enrolling as an organisation, so a D-U-N-S was simply required. The GSTIN supplied on 2026-08-18 carries a PAN whose fourth character is **`P` — an individual, a sole proprietorship** — where the previous entity's was `F`, a firm.\n\nA D-U-N-S number is only needed for **organisation** enrolment. Whether a sole proprietorship can enrol as an organisation on Apple and Google, and what evidence each wants, is the open question — see `../people/owner-store-account-entity.md`. Filing the D-U-N-S before that is answered risks either wasted effort or, worse, an application describing the entity wrongly.\n\nIf organisation enrolment turns out to be available, one number still serves both stores and this record proceeds unchanged. If it is not, the apps publish under a personal name and Google requires new personal accounts to run a closed test with a dozen testers before production.\n\n**The evidence shifted on 2026-08-19, and the hold is now a choice rather than a necessity.** Field reports folded into `../people/owner-store-account-entity.md` show sole proprietors obtaining organisation enrolment on both stores — Google directly, Apple via a manual support unlock, with one Indian confirmation — and D&B registering proprietorships as proprietorships. That removes the worst risk this hold was protecting against: an application *describing the entity wrongly* is avoided by filing it as what it is, a sole proprietorship under the proprietor's legal name with Convenience Corner as trade name. What the hold still protects is smaller: if the owner chose individual enrolment anyway, a free application was filed unnecessarily. Filing early buys back the longest lead time in the plan; the decision is the owner's, made with the question record's ask.\n\n**Which lead time applies to Meghalaya is unknown.** The plan plans for 30 days and finishes early if it is five — not the other way round.\n\n## How to file (decided 2026-08-19)\n\nThe route is **Apple's D-U-N-S tool, and it is free** — verified against Apple's own D-U-N-S support page on 2026-08-19, which states the request is free, quotes up to **5 business days** for D&B to issue and **2 more business days** for the number to reach Apple's systems, and says to email D&B if it runs past two weeks (their Apple-dedicated support portal is `support.dnb.com/?CUST=APPLEDEV`). This record still budgets 30 days, and finishes early if Apple's figure holds.\n\n1. **Search before filing.** Sign in to the D-U-N-S Lookup at `developer.apple.com/enroll/duns-lookup/` (any Apple Account works) and search for the business first — registrations sometimes seed a D&B listing, and a duplicate filing is the one avoidable mess. If a number already exists, this record skips to *granted* and only the profile details need checking.\n2. **If nothing is found, the same tool offers the free request.** Submit with the details below.\n3. **Expect a verification contact from D&B** — an email (check the sender's domain is `dnb.com` before acting on it) or a call, asking for things like business type and employee count. Apple's page says to have business registration documents ready; here that is the GST certificate. Reply promptly — the clock runs on their side.\n4. **Pay nobody.** The Apple-routed number is free. D&B also sells paid/expedited products and third-party agents in India charge for \"D-U-N-S assistance\" — decline both; neither is needed for either store.\n5. **When the number arrives**, fill `submitted_on` / `reference` / `granted_on` above, append dated lines below, and then organisation enrolment can start — expecting Apple's legal-entity refusal and using the reshaped ask in `../people/owner-store-account-entity.md` (support verifies the D-U-N-S and unlocks). **One number serves both stores**; Google Play's organisation verification reads the same record.\n\n**Details to have ready — and they must match the GST certificate exactly**, because both stores match the D-U-N-S record against entity documents, and a mismatch here becomes a re-verification later:\n\n| Field | What to enter |\n|---|---|\n| Legal entity name | The **proprietor's own legal name**, exactly as on the PAN / GST certificate — a proprietorship has no separate legal personality, so the legal name is the person's |\n| Trade name / doing-business-as | **Convenience Corner**, as the GST certificate records it |\n| Headquarters address | The business address as on the GST certificate — physical address in Tura, Meghalaya, with PIN |\n| Mailing address | Same, or the real one if different |\n| Work contact | Proprietor's name, role (Proprietor), business phone, and a **durable business email** — this is where D&B's verification email lands, and ideally the same address the store accounts will use |\n| Ready for the verification call | GST registration certificate (carries all three of the above), PAN, business type (retail — convenience store), year established (2026), approximate employee count |\n\nThe GSTIN itself and its verification live in `design-system/pages/admin.md` §5 and are not restated here.\n\n## Where it stands\n\nNot started. Nothing has been submitted.\n\n2026-08-19 — Field evidence (see `../people/owner-store-account-entity.md`) points to the D-U-N-S being needed after all: organisation enrolment is attainable for proprietorships via Apple support. The do-not-file hold is now a trade-off, not a cliff — see above.\n\n2026-08-19 (later) — **Hold lifted by the owner's decision: file as a sole proprietorship.** Filing steps and the details checklist recorded above (§How to file), verified against Apple's D-U-N-S support page the same day. Awaiting the owner starting the lookup; the verification email will arrive from D&B's domain.\n\n*Append dated lines here as things happen. Do not rewrite history — a wrong assumption you can see is worth more than a tidy record.*",
